---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, TRACKING } from '../../config.js';
const tracks = Boolean(TRACKING.metaPixelId || TRACKING.ga4Id);
---
<Base title={`Privacy and cookies | ${SITE.name}`} description="What The Style News collects, why, and how to change your mind.">
  <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
  <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
  <div class="body">
    <p>The short version: we don't collect anything about you unless you say yes,
    and saying no changes nothing about how the site works.</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is published by <strong>Son of John B.V.</strong>, Keizersstraat 32,
    Amsterdam, the Netherlands. For any question about this site or your data,
    contact us via <a href={SITE.publisherUrl}>sonofjohnlabel.com</a>.</p>

    {tracks ? (
      <>
        <h2>What we'd like to set, and why</h2>
        <p>If you accept, we load measurement tools that tell us whether our
        advertising is working — roughly, how many people who saw an ad went on to
        read an article or click through to a shop. They set cookies in your
        browser and share data with the companies that provide them.</p>
        <p>We load nothing until you choose. If you decline, or simply ignore the
        banner, none of it runs.</p>

        <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
        <p>You can withdraw or change your choice at any time. It takes effect
        immediately and we forget what you picked before.</p>
        <p><button type="button" class="cta" onclick="window.tsnResetConsent && window.tsnResetConsent()">
          Change my cookie choice
        </button></p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>What we set right now</h2>
        <p>Nothing. This site currently loads no analytics, no advertising pixels
        and no third-party scripts of any kind, and sets no cookies. If that
        changes we'll ask before anything runs.</p>
      </>
    )}

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Articles marked as partner content link to <a href={SITE.publisherUrl}>Son of John</a>.
    Once you follow a link you're on their site, under their privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the GDPR you can ask what we hold about you, ask us to correct or
    delete it, and complain to the Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens if you think we've
    got it wrong. Get in touch with us first and we'll try to sort it out.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
